# Keeps the Scenario_Player/ build context small. The Dockerfile's COPY list is what actually
# decides what lands in an image - this file only stops useless bytes being uploaded to the builder,
# and makes the "never in the image" rule explicit for the paths that could be mistaken for app
# code.
#
# Do NOT add codec_helper/ here: stage 1 builds cpm_encode from it. Only its local build tree is
# excluded, below.

# Test code and fixtures - stage 2 runs no tests, and the golden .uper/.json corpus is CI/pytest
# input only (requirements-dev.txt, which installs pytest + jsonschema, is excluded too).
tests/
requirements-dev.txt

# Documentation is never part of the image (node-code-layout.md: doc/ is documentation only);
# README.md is the folder's human guide, same category.
doc/
README.md

# A local developer build tree of the helper - _deps alone holds the whole Vanetza clone plus its
# object files, i.e. gigabytes of context for nothing. Stage 1 configures its own build/ inside the
# image, so a host-built one must never be uploaded (or shadow it).
codec_helper/build/

# Python bytecode from local test runs - stale, platform-specific, and would ride along in
# COPY player/.
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
